    content: "## 🚀 The Real Deal on Event-Driven Architecture and Pub/Sub Pattern\n\n> Horizontal scaling and load balancing keep services reliable under high traffic.\n\nIf you've been working in tech for a while, you've probably seen this done poorly. Let's fix that.\n\n### Why it actually matters:\n- **Performance:** Start with requirements: scale, latency SLA, consistency needs, and read/write ratio.\n- **Reliability:** Design for failure — every component will eventually fail; plan for it.\n### The Right Way\n\n```js\n// Rate limiter using Token Bucket (conceptual)\nclass TokenBucket {\n  constructor(capacity, refillRatePerSec) {\n    this.capacity = capacity;\n    this.tokens = capacity;\n    this.refillRate = refillRatePerSec;\n    setInterval(() => { this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + this.refillRate); }, 1000);\n  }\n  consume() { if (this.tokens > 0) { this.tokens--; return true; } return false; }\n}\n```\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n👉 **Takeaway:** Great system design is about asking the right questions and making explicit trade-offs."
