    content: "## ⚡ How Backtracking: Subsets Permutations Combinations Saved Our Architecture\n\nSix months ago, our system was buckling under the pressure.\n\n**The Turning Point:** We re-evaluated our core assumptions.\n\n**The Fix:** Recursion and dynamic programming convert exponential problems into polynomial ones.\n\nWe completely rethought our approach. Instead of fighting the framework, we embraced the native patterns.\n### What we wrote:\n\n```js\n// Two Sum — O(n) using hash map\nfunction twoSum(nums, target) {\n  const map = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n    const complement = target - nums[i];\n    if (map[complement] !== undefined) return [map[complement], i];\n    map[nums[i]] = i;\n  }\n  return [];\n}\n```\n\n### The Outcome\nPerformance improved dramatically. Use hash maps to trade space for time in lookup-heavy problems..\n\n\n---\n\n\n👉 **Lesson Learned:** Master the tradeoff between time and space — that is the DSA interview edge."
